Test that migrate options are correctly passed down, also when migrating
dependent resources.

The test scenario is:
- vm:101, ct:102, vm:103, ct:104, vm:105 and ct:106 are all currently running on
  node1.
- vm:101 and ct:102 are migrated to node2 with a guest-type-specific
  migration option and a common migration option.
- vm:103, ct:104, vm:105 and ct:106 are kept together via a positive affinity
  rule.
- vm:103 is migrated to node2 with a vm-specific and a common migration option.
- ct:104 is migrated to node3 with a ct-specific and a common migration option.

The expected outcome is:
- vm:101 and ct:102 end up on node2.
- vm:103, ct:104, vm:105 and ct:106 all end up on node3.
- The guest-type-specific migration option is passed down for the matching guest
  type and the common migration option is always passed down, also when
  migrating dependent resources.
